Unit proof for escape over all printable strings up to length 3
(length arithmetic; unescape round-trip).  KNOWNBUG: the propositional
reduction runs out of memory (16 GiB) -- escape's incremental
`result += c` performs data-dependent heap reallocation, and dynamic
objects with symbolic size explode in bit-blasting (same class as
bigint_arith; see the stage-profiling findings).  Flip to CORE when
the encoding scales (SMT array backend or capacity-bounded string
model).
